From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 21:36:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hand a console-sender command dispatch to the global region

Folia's CraftServer.dispatchCommand branches on the sender: an Entity sender
requires that entity's region, a console/RCON sender requires the global region.
A plugin handling a player event is on a region thread, so dispatching a command
AS THE CONSOLE - which is how reward commands are almost always written - throws
out of the event handler and everything after that line is skipped. Measured:
LycoQuest's reward grant failed 7/7 that way.

The parse stays on the calling thread and only the execution is handed to the
global region, so Paper's only false (no such command) is preserved verbatim and
returned synchronously. Parsing there is not a new exposure: Commands guards the
dispatcher with no thread check, parse is a read-only walk of the Brigadier tree,
and VanillaCommandWrapper.tabComplete does the same getListener+parse pair off
the global thread today; the console CommandSourceStack reads server-level
respawn data, not chunk or block state.

This is not "route arbitrary work to the global scheduler": the owner is not
inferred - the ensureGlobalTickThread call this replaces is the platform stating
that the global region is where a console sender executes - and an Entity sender
is untouched, so it is not all commands either. Only a thread that is ticking a
region hands off; a thread with no observable context is still refused, exactly
as stock.

Not preserved: an exception thrown during execution no longer propagates out of
the dispatchCommand call. Of 62 dispatch callsites in this plugin set, 57 discard
the return value and the only real branch on it is in a BungeeCord proxy class
the server never loads.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
index 88d03cecae2861c263dfe9334af338d08db98b1c..6bd1ef83af4c6e4d28b258a563fe1795511c4b6a 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
@@ -948,6 +948,12 @@ public final class CraftServer implements Server {
         } else if (rawSender instanceof ConsoleCommandSender || rawSender instanceof net.minecraft.server.rcon.RconConsoleSource
                 || rawSender instanceof org.bukkit.craftbukkit.command.CraftRemoteConsoleCommandSender
                 || rawSender instanceof io.papermc.paper.commands.FeedbackForwardingSender) {
+            // Lophinya start - hand a console-sender dispatch to the region that sender belongs to
+            if (fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaCommandDispatch.shouldHandOff()) {
+                return fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaCommandDispatch.handOff(rawSender, commandLine,
+                    () -> this.dispatchCommand(rawSender, commandLine));
+            }
+            // Lophinya end
             io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.RegionizedServer.ensureGlobalTickThread("Dispatching command async");
         } else {
             // huh?
